<!--
  Extra pain-voice wave slots for TacePatch's [PAINVOICE] feature.

  Paste these <Slot> blocks into pc/audio/config/waveslots.xml, inside the
  top-level <WaveSlots> element. Order does not matter: the game reads the file
  into a hash table keyed by Name.

  One pair per configured voice, numbered by the Voice<N> ini key:

      Voice1  ->  PAIN_EXTRA_0_0 / PAIN_EXTRA_0_1
      Voice2  ->  PAIN_EXTRA_1_0 / PAIN_EXTRA_1_1
      Voice3  ->  PAIN_EXTRA_2_0 / PAIN_EXTRA_2_1
      Voice4  ->  PAIN_EXTRA_3_0 / PAIN_EXTRA_3_1

  Sizes match the stock NIKO_0 / NIKO_1 pain slots, which are the largest of the
  vanilla pain banks - 172032 bytes each, so a pair costs 336 KB of audio heap.
  The heap is sized from the sum of every slot in this file, so adding slots
  grows it rather than squeezing the existing ones.

  A pair that is missing here is not fatal: TacePatch logs it and leaves those
  peds on the generic PAIN_MALE / PAIN_FEMALE voice.
-->

  <Slot>
    <Name content="ascii">PAIN_EXTRA_0_0</Name>
    <MaxHeaderSize value="59392" />
    <LoadType content="ascii">BANK</LoadType>
    <Size value="172032" />
  </Slot>
  <Slot>
    <Name content="ascii">PAIN_EXTRA_0_1</Name>
    <MaxHeaderSize value="59392" />
    <LoadType content="ascii">BANK</LoadType>
    <Size value="172032" />
  </Slot>
  <Slot>
    <Name content="ascii">PAIN_EXTRA_1_0</Name>
    <MaxHeaderSize value="59392" />
    <LoadType content="ascii">BANK</LoadType>
    <Size value="172032" />
  </Slot>
  <Slot>
    <Name content="ascii">PAIN_EXTRA_1_1</Name>
    <MaxHeaderSize value="59392" />
    <LoadType content="ascii">BANK</LoadType>
    <Size value="172032" />
  </Slot>
